    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the membership-level rule with the points system.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 split the logic into two small, cohesive static methods:\n   - `points(...)` \u2014 computes points: `+2` email present, `+1` namesakeCount 0, `+2` household \u2265 3, `+3` tenure > 365 days (reusing the existing tenure helper, renamed `exceedsTenure`).\n   - `of(int points)` \u2014 maps points to level: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping via `MembershipLevel.points(...)` and re-pointed `membershipLevel` at `MembershipLevel.of(points(...))`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel` (description + `maximum: 4`) so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes both fields.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** I kept behaviour in the small, self-contained `MembershipLevel` class rather than growing the mapper or a large class \u2014 every changed/added method is short with low surrounding complexity (low WMC_other), and I touched only the three files the change fundamentally requires. The verified test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh email-only owner) passes.",
