    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered flow for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:102-137`).\n\n## 1. Security check (before the method runs)\n- `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected.\n\n## 2. Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid @RequestBody`, `OwnersApi.java:86`)\nRuns before the method body; any failure \u2192 **400 Bad Request**. From `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n- **firstName**: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, 1\u20133 space/`'`/`-`-separated words), `@Size(1..30)`\n- **lastName**: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n- **address**: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (must contain a non-blank char), `@Size(1..255)`\n- **city**: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n- **telephone**: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (E.164 / national formats), `@Size(1..20)`, plus custom `@E164NationalLength` \u2014 after E.164 normalization, national digits must match the country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210)\n- **email** (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`, plus custom `@NonDisposableEmail` \u2014 rejects `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`\n- **postcode** (optional): `@Pattern(\"^\\\\d{4}$\")`\n- **registrationDate** (optional): `@PastOrPresent`\n- **birthDate** (optional): `@PastOrPresent`\n- **class-level `@ValidPostcode`**: if a postcode is present *and* the city maps to a known region (`Locality.of(city)` \u2192 NSW/VIC/QLD), the postcode must fall in that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown region or blank/non-4-digit postcode is accepted.\n\n## 3. Method body \u2014 side-effects and business rules, in execution order\n\n1. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, MapStruct via setters), which normalizes as a side-effect:\n   - `setAddress` \u2192 `AddressNormalizer.normalize`: trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST`/`RD`/`AVE` \u2192 `STREET`/`ROAD`/`AVENUE`\n   - `setTelephone` \u2192 `PhoneNumbers.toE164`: strip non-digits, assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` when no `+`\n   - `setEmail` \u2192 lowercased\n   - `id` and `pets` ignored\n2. **Resolve registration date**: use the supplied `registrationDate` or `LocalDate.now()`, then `BusinessDay.adjust` (a Sat/Sun rolls forward to Monday); store it on the owner.\n3. **Load all existing owners** (`clinicService.findAllOwners()`).\n4. **Daily-volume check**: if \u2265 100 existing owners share the same (adjusted) registration date \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests** (no save).\n5. **Identity / city-cap conflict**: if any existing owner has the same `identityKey` (normalized `telephone|email|`) **OR** \u2265 50 existing owners share the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409 Conflict** (no save).\n6. **Set `namesakeCount`** = number of existing owners with the same first *and* last name (case-insensitive).\n7. **Household conflict**: if any existing owner is in the same household (same `householdId` = hash of last name + postcode) *and* the request's `sharesHousehold` is not `true` \u2192 **409 Conflict** (no save). (Never fires when postcode is null, since `householdId` is then null.)\n8. **Set `householdMemberCount`** = 1 + number of existing owners in the same household.\n9. **Set `customerCode`** = `CustomerCode.of(...)` \u2192 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region resolved postcode-first then city; hash of telephone + last name).\n10. **Set `possibleDuplicate = false`** and **`possibleDuplicateOf = null`** (explicitly, overriding the field's documented semantics).\n11. **Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`), which triggers JPA lifecycle callbacks:\n    - `@PrePersist Owner.defaultRegistrationDate()` \u2014 defaults registration date if null (already set here, so a no-op)\n    - `@PostPersist OwnerAuditListener.onCreate` \u2014 logs to the `AUDIT` logger: id, customerCode, registrationDate\n12. **Map to `OwnerDto`** (`ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`), deriving `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `telephoneDisplay`, `ageBand`.\n13. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** on the DTO = whether > 80 of the *pre-existing* owners share this registration date.\n14. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n15. **Return 201 Created** with the DTO body and headers.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging as you read this: the three short-circuit business rules (steps 4, 5, 7) return their status *after* the entity has already been normalized but *before* any save, and the `bulkSignupWarning` in step 13 counts the pre-existing owners only (the just-saved owner is not in the `owners` collection)."
